  "question": {
    "text": "Lines $x+y=1$ and $3 y=x+3$ intersect the ellipse $x^{2}+9 y^{2}=9$ at the points $P, Q$ and $R$. The area of the $\\triangle P Q R$ is",
    "image": null
  },
  "options": [
    {
      "id": "CDBLD",
      "text": "$\\frac{36}{5}$",
      "isCorrect": false,
      "image": null
    },
    {
      "id": "uBcQz",
      "text": "$\\frac{18}{5}$",
      "isCorrect": true,
      "image": null
    },
    {
      "id": "9Pl2H",
      "text": "$\\frac{9}{5}$",
      "isCorrect": false,
      "image": null
    },
    {
      "id": "sKtKh",
      "text": "$\\frac{1}{5}$",
      "isCorrect": false,
      "image": null
    }
  ],
  "correctValue": null,
  "solution": {
    "text": "Given equation of ellipse\r\n$$\r\nx^{2}+9 y^{2}=9\r\n$$\r\n$\\Rightarrow \\quad \\frac{x^{2}}{9}+\\frac{y^{2}}{1}=1$\r\nand equation of lines\r\n$$\r\nx+y=1 \\text { and } 3 y=x+3\r\n$$\r\nor $\\quad \\frac{x}{(-3)}+\\frac{y}{1}=1$\r\n<img src=\"https://cdn-question-pool.getmarks.app/pyq/wbjee/2013_mat_a4.png\">\r\n\r\n$\\therefore$ Area of $\\Delta P Q R=\\left|\\begin{array}{c|ccc}0 & 1 & 1 \\\\ -3 & 0 & 1 \\\\ 9 / 5 & -4 / 5 & 1\\end{array}\\right| \\mid$\r\n$=\\frac{1}{2}\\left[\\frac{24}{5}+\\frac{12}{5}\\right]$\r\n$=\\frac{1}{2} \\times \\frac{36}{5}=\\frac{18}{5}$",
    "image": null
  },
